refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
boolshm_remove SysvSharedMemoryshm
shm_remove marks the shared memory segment shm for destruction. The segment is destroyed, and its data with it, when the last process attached to it detaches. The key is released immediately: a later call to shm_attach with the same key creates a new, empty segment. Until the old segment is destroyed, shm and the processes already attached to it can keep reading and writing it.

&reftitle.parameters;


  shm


    A shared memory segment obtained from shm_attach.

&reftitle.returnvalues;

 &return.success;
 An E_WARNING is raised when the removal is refused,
 typically because the segment belongs to another user.

&reftitle.errors;

 Throws an Error if shm has
 already been detached with shm_detach.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.0.0

     shm expects a SysvSharedMemory
     instance now; previously, a resource was expected.
